or maybe if that is too "magic" then the gen_id method could accept the assembled seed string, so in use it would look like:

```
def gen_trace_id(dag_run: DagRun, as_int: bool = False) -> str | int:
    seed = f"{dag_run.dag_id}_{dag_run.run_id}_{dag_run.start_date.timestamp()}"
    return gen_id(seed, as_int, shorten=False)
```

Either of those would reduce around 50 lines of repetitive code with around 20 lines, and be just as easy to read (IMHO), easier to modify later if all of those needs to get changed at some point, and just as easy to change if only one needs to get adjusted later.  No disadvantage IMHO.

